+# Decisions: the lab's role, where issues live, the processes kept, and how work merges
+
+Justin's decisions of 25 September to 4 October 2026, copied on 2026-10-07 from `STATE.md` as updated
+2026-10-04 17:31. `STATE.md` is overwritten at each verified event, and a search of this Scope (`decisions/`,
+`memory/`, `reports/`) and of ORC's documents and code found these recorded nowhere else. GitHub issues could not be
+read for the search. The words below are `STATE.md`'s, with its attributions; copying them here is not deciding them
+again.
+
+## Justin, 4 October 2026, afternoon (interview)
+
+- **The lab is the central Scope** for project management, core issue tracking, code quality and security. Astra is to
+  say what else it should cover.
+- **Where issues live:** a Scope's issues stay in its own repository, on one central map; a `core` label marks a Scope
+  issue that needs ORC's core changed. Later, Scopes may track their own business logic elsewhere.
+- **The processes kept, all of them:**
+  - map and label check;
+  - tests on every PR (#144);
+  - the security-review and package-API checks;
+  - daily diary;
+  - weekly adversarial review;
+  - entropy guard at session end;
+  - FRICTION into rules, monthly (#60);
+  - branch and worktree cleanup (#70);
+  - `/tmp` cleanup (#182).
+- **ORC scheduling (#166) is built first,** and the scheduled ones run through it.
+- **Astra runs entropy-guard's assessment on ORC and the lab together.** Justin is shaping the brief before it runs.
+- **Labels:** the type-label proposal waits on Astra's revisions (`reports/2026-10-04-labels-review-astra.md`).
+
+## Justin, 4 October 2026
+
+- **MS is paused:** browser-stack work that touches it (#118, #52, MS #52) waits.
+
+## Justin, 2 October 2026
+
+- **Git cleanup moved to Worktrunk and gh poi** (Justin: "yes"). `git-tidy-report` is deleted (local-config
+  `4811698`); `wt` and `gh poi` come from local-config `scripts/install-git-tools.sh`.
+- **Security reviews are checked on GitHub by Danger** (Justin: "B"). orchestrator #179 and MS #49: a pull request
+  changing a guarded path fails the "Security review" check until its description has a `## Security review` section.
+  ORC's `dangerfile.js` also records this decision in its header.
+
+## Justin, 25 September 2026
+
+- **Claude merges a PR once review and tests pass;** a review posted on the PR plus Justin's go-ahead gets past Claude
+  Code's classifier.
